<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine II of Greece</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> was the last king of Greece, reigning from 1964. He clashed with the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgios-papandreou">Georgios Papandreou</a> and accepted the colonels' coup of April 1967, but his failed counter-coup that December forced him into exile. The junta abolished the monarchy in 1973, and a referendum in 1974 confirmed the republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-ii-of-greece.jpg" alt="Constantine II of Greece" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allan warren; derivative work by Daffy123 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Constantine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
